Id: sysd006f
Severity: FAIL
Category: services
Check: check_units
References: systemd.unit(5)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-5, CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

A file an enabled systemd service is made of (its unit file or a
drop-in, as 'systemctl cat' lists them), or a directory above it, is
not root's alone: it belongs to another account, or its group or
anyone can write it. Whoever can change the unit decides what the
service runs, and as whom: an ExecStart= of their own runs as root at
the next start or daemon-reload.

To fix it, 'chown root:root' the file and 'chmod 644' it (go-w on the
directory), and find out who changed it.
